== the rule, pure ==
the bound is reached at three samples of a third of it, not at two: true
a window just short of the bound is not ended: true
a sixteen-sample window under the bound is not ended: true
a dispersed window is not ended, however long: true
the gate keeps a minimum under it from ending the window, and admits one at it: true
no finite positive minimum, no early end: true
== the sampling loop ==
a slow window ends at three samples under the bound: true
... and takes its whole sixteen-sample floor without it: true
a fast window keeps its floor under the bound: true
the caller's repeats still wins: five repeats take five slow samples: true
a resumed window that already meets the bound takes no fresh sample: true
== executed cc searches ==
isolated: a slow baseline's window ended at three samples: true
isolated: ... admitted and ranked at its reading: true
isolated: every other window, timed beside it, took its whole floor: true
isolated: a fast baseline's window took its whole floor: true
queued: a slow baseline's window ended at three samples: true
queued: ... admitted and ranked at its reading: true
queued: every other window, timed beside it, took its whole floor: true
queued: a fast baseline's window took its whole floor: true
autotune_baseline_window: done
